# A save this build will not open: what the player is told, through the real keys.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/saves-elsewhere.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0
#
# A save keeps only its seed and grows the world again when it is opened, so a
# build whose landscape registry has moved makes a DIFFERENT island from that
# seed (adding salt_flats and scrapwood moved 9% of every world's tiles). The
# save is not opened onto ground that moved; it is named, and the reason is on
# the glass. This tour writes its own saves through the app's own keys and then
# ages them with `stale`, because no boot flag can fake a save an older build
# wrote and a save written by hand would not be the same file.
#
# Both lines of the guard are walked:
#   slot 1, `stale version`   -> a file with no stamp at all, what every save on
#                                a player's disk today is: refused before it boots
#   slot 2, `stale landscape` -> the stamp still this build's, the ground under it
#                                moved: caught only once the world is grown, so
#                                the game hands back to the title with the reason
coast calm
# Walk first, and shoot the world, before anything is pressed. The runner gives
# the loading page 30 s to lift and then goes on regardless; pausing while it is
# still up stops the game the page is waiting on, and the page never lifts, so
# every frame after it is a picture of the page. Walking is real input that
# costs real seconds and cannot do that, and 00 is the frame that says the world
# is up: if it is the loading page, the machine is too loaded to prove anything
# and the run is not evidence.
wait 2
walk 1,0 1.5
walk -1,0 1.5
shot 00-standing-in-the-world with land:coast
wait 1
tap pause
wait 1
choose saves
tap use
await app:saves 4
wait 0.4
# Two saves of this game, both this build's, both of this island. An empty slot
# is written at once; one an earlier run of this tour left asks first, and the
# second press writes over it.
choose slot_1
try 2
tap use
await saved 2
end
wait 0.5
choose slot_2
try 2
tap use
await saved 2
end
wait 0.5
# Slot 1 goes back to a file from before the stamp existed.
stale 1 version
# Right turns the app from saving to loading, and reads the slots again.
tap move_right
wait 0.5
choose slot_1
wait 0.5
# The game is still there — its picture, its day, where it stood — and under it
# the whole reason this build will not open it.
shot 01-another-island with app:saves
tap use
wait 0.8
# Pressing load anyway: refused, and said again on the key strip.
shot 02-refused with app:saves
# Slot 2 was written by THIS build, on THIS island, and still opens: nothing was
# broken for the saves that are still this world's.
choose slot_2
wait 0.4
shot 03-the-one-that-still-opens with app:saves
tap use
await game 30
coast calm
# A load starts its own loading page, so the same rule holds here: walk in the
# world that came back before shooting it.
walk 1,0 1.5
walk -1,0 1.5
wait 4
shot 04-loaded with land:coast
# --- the second line: ground that moved under a save the stamp cannot see -----
# No stamp can see into the worldgen stages, so this is caught only after the
# world has been grown and the game is already booting. It does not play on: it
# takes no save of its own, and hands back to the title.
stale 2 landscape
tap pause
wait 1
choose saves
tap use
await app:saves 4
wait 0.4
tap move_right
wait 0.5
choose slot_2
wait 0.4
tap use
await title 40
wait 2
# The title, with the whole reason on its glass in the same amber the saves app
# says it in — not a line in the key strip the player cannot read the rest of.
shot 05-handed-back with title
key pause
wait 1
# Back on the list. Continue is faded: slot 1 has no stamp, slot 2 is the one
# this build has just tried and turned away, and nothing else holds a game.
shot 06-continue-faded with title
key move_down
key use
wait 1
# And the whole reason comes back whenever it is asked for, so a player whose
# only save is one of these is never left with a row they cannot press and no
# account of why.
shot 07-the-reason-again with title
